WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:06.275
Lab 1 runs in the lifecycle extensions folder
of the examples, and nothing signs in.

3
00:00:06.275 --> 00:00:09.891
Step one extracts Learn's
definition from the pinned page,

4
00:00:09.891 --> 00:00:12.075
and lints it with a one-hour timeout.

5
00:00:12.075 --> 00:00:14.488
Eight results, and exit code two.

6
00:00:14.488 --> 00:00:19.450
Five are findings: it hard-codes the
worldwide Graph host, calls back on beta,

7
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.331
uses the callback path
without checking it,

8
00:00:22.331 --> 00:00:26.813
sends no callback when the work
fails, and always reports completed.

9
00:00:26.813 --> 00:00:31.512
Two warnings are for run history, and
one for the implicit retry policy.

10
00:00:31.512 --> 00:00:35.874
Step two runs Learn's definition
for a GCC High tenant.

11
00:00:35.874 --> 00:00:40.323
The one POST goes to the worldwide
Graph, on beta, and the last line

12
00:00:40.323 --> 00:00:45.275
is what Lifecycle Workflows records:
failed, no callback within an hour.

13
00:00:45.275 --> 00:00:49.500
So a GCC High leaver's task
fails at the end of the wait.

14
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.300
Run it again for a worldwide
tenant, and the task is completed.
